%% SovereignAI Edge - User Request Flow (Chat Completion)
%% Sequence diagram showing the complete chat request lifecycle

sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    actor User
    participant Client as Client (Web/Electron/CLI)
    participant Gateway as FastAPI Gateway (127.0.0.1:8000)
    participant Middleware as Middleware Stack
    participant ChatAPI as POST /v1/chat/completions
    participant Settings as SettingsService
    participant VectorStore as VectorStore (RAG)
    participant Template as apply_chat_template
    participant ModelMgr as ModelManager
    participant EngineFactory as EngineFactory
    participant TaskResolver as TaskResolver
    participant MemoryMgr as MemoryManager
    participant Engine as Active Engine (FullRAM/LayerStream)
    participant Transformers as transformers / PyTorch
    participant SSE as SSE Stream Response

    Note over User, SSE: === CHAT REQUEST FLOW ===
    
    User->>Client: Types message, hits Enter
    Client->>Gateway: POST /v1/chat/completions<br/>{model, messages, stream:true, temperature...}
    Gateway->>Middleware: CORS → Auth(conditional) → RateLimit → Logging
    Middleware->>ChatAPI: Request validated, forwarded
    
    Note over ChatAPI, Settings: --- PRE-PROCESSING ---
    ChatAPI->>Settings: get_system_prompt()
    Settings-->>ChatAPI: System prompt string
    ChatAPI->>VectorStore: build_context(top_k=5) [if RAG enabled]
    VectorStore-->>ChatAPI: RAG context chunks
    ChatAPI->>Template: apply_chat_template(messages + system + RAG, enable_thinking)
    Template-->>ChatAPI: Formatted prompt tokens
    
    Note over ChatAPI, Engine: --- MODEL LOAD / ENGINE SELECTION ---
    alt Model not loaded or mode mismatch
        ChatAPI->>ModelMgr: load_model(model_id, mode="auto")
        ModelMgr->>ModelMgr: _fuzzy_match_model() → base model path
        ModelMgr->>ModelMgr: _load_model_locked() (asyncio.Lock)
        ModelMgr->>EngineFactory: create_engine(model_path, mode="auto")
        EngineFactory->>EngineFactory: Compute model size (params × bytes)
        EngineFactory->>TaskResolver: resolve(model_path)
        TaskResolver->>TaskResolver: AutoConfig.from_pretrained()
        TaskResolver-->>EngineFactory: {task_type, is_generative, architecture}
        EngineFactory->>MemoryMgr: suggest_mode(model_size, hw_profile)
        MemoryMgr->>MemoryMgr: llmfit.score_model_fit() → fit_score
        alt fit > 0.85 AND RAM < 70%
            MemoryMgr-->>EngineFactory: "fullram"
        else if fit > 0.6
            MemoryMgr-->>EngineFactory: "layerstream"
        else
            MemoryMgr->>MemoryMgr: Threshold fallback (VRAM/RAM ratios)
            MemoryMgr-->>EngineFactory: "fullram" | "layerstream" | "insufficient"
        end
        EngineFactory-->>ModelMgr: Engine instance (FullRAM/LayerStream)
        ModelMgr->>Engine: engine.load()
        Note right of Engine: FullRAM: AutoModelForCausalLM.load()<br/>LayerStream: WeightSplitter + LayerLoader init
        Engine-->>ModelMgr: Loaded + memory usage
        ModelMgr->>ModelMgr: app.state.active_engine = engine<br/>app.state.active_model = model_id<br/>app.state.active_mode = mode
    else Model already loaded
        ModelMgr-->>ChatAPI: Existing active_engine
    end
    
    Note over ChatAPI, Engine: --- GENERATION ---
    alt Streaming (stream=true)
        ChatAPI->>Engine: generate_stream(input_data, **gen_kwargs)
        Note right of Engine: FullRAM: TextIteratorStreamer thread<br/>LayerStream: _gen_loop thread (prefill→decode)
        Engine-->>ChatAPI: AsyncGenerator[Dict]
        ChatAPI->>SSE: stream_response() generator
        Note right of SSE: _split_think() → reasoning separation<br/>_trim_tag_prefix() → think tag cleanup<br/>~96 chars/frame batching<br/>is_disconnected() check
        loop For each token chunk
            SSE-->>Client: SSE: data: {token, ...}\n\n
            Client->>User: Render token incrementally
        end
        SSE-->>Client: SSE: data: [DONE]\n\n
    else Non-streaming (stream=false)
        ChatAPI->>Engine: generate(input_data, **gen_kwargs)
        Engine->>Transformers: model.generate() (in thread pool)
        Transformers-->>Engine: Complete token IDs
        Engine-->>ChatAPI: {text, usage, finish_reason}
        ChatAPI-->>Client: JSON Response
        Client->>User: Render complete response
    end
    
    Note over User, SSE: === MODE SWITCH FLOW (POST /v1/chat/mode/switch) ===
    User->>Client: Request mode switch (fullram/layerstream/auto)
    Client->>Gateway: POST /v1/chat/mode/switch?mode=layerstream
    Gateway->>ChatAPI: Route to mode switch handler
    ChatAPI->>ModelMgr: load_model(current_model, mode="layerstream")
    ModelMgr->>ModelMgr: Unload current engine (engine.unload())
    ModelMgr->>EngineFactory: create_engine(model_path, mode="layerstream")
    EngineFactory->>MemoryMgr: suggest_mode() [re-evaluates]
    MemoryMgr-->>EngineFactory: Mode decision
    EngineFactory-->>ModelMgr: New LayerStreamEngine
    ModelMgr->>Engine: engine.load()
    Engine-->>ModelMgr: Ready
    ModelMgr->>ModelMgr: Update app.state.active_*
    ModelMgr-->>ChatAPI: {mode, model, status}
    ChatAPI-->>Client: JSON Response
    Client->>User: "Mode switched to LayerStream"
    
    Note over User, SSE: === BENCHMARK FLOW (POST /v1/system/benchmark) ===
    User->>Client: Run benchmark
    Client->>Gateway: POST /v1/system/benchmark {model, prompts, mode}
    Gateway->>SystemRouter: Route to benchmark endpoint
    SystemRouter->>ModelMgr: load_model(model, mode)
    SystemRouter->>Engine: generate() × N prompts
    Engine-->>SystemRouter: Latency, tokens/sec, peak RAM
    SystemRouter->>DatabaseManager: INSERT benchmark_results
    SystemRouter-->>Client: Benchmark results
    Client->>User: Display metrics

